# Elixir Practice

## Strings

```elixir
name="Octallium"
```

```elixir
"Octallium"=name
```

```elixir
<<head,rest::binary>> = name
head
```

```elixir
rest
```

```elixir
head==?O
```

```elixir
<<"Oct", rest::binary>>=name
rest
```

## CharList

```elixir
greet = 'Hello'
```

```elixir
greet ++ ' Everyone'
```

```elixir
is_list(greet)
```

## List

```elixir
ls = ["a","b","c"]
```

```elixir
Enum.at(ls,0)
```

```elixir
[one,two,three]=ls
one
```

```elixir
[_,middle,_]=ls
middle
#Ignores any value in between
```

```elixir
[h|t] = ls
h
```

```elixir
t
```

## Tuple

```elixir
tp={1,2}
```

```elixir
{a,b}=tp
```

```elixir
a
```

```elixir
{:reply,msg}={:reply,"Not Found"}
```

## Keyword List

```elixir
kls=[a: 1,b: 2]
```

```elixir
[{:a,1},{:b,2}]=[a: 1,b: 2]
```

```elixir
kls[:a]
```

## Map

```elixir
my_map=%{a: 1,b: 2}
```

```elixir
%{a: first}=my_map
first
```

```elixir
%{a: first, b: second}
second
```

```elixir
map2 = %{"a" => 1, "b" => 2}
```

```elixir
%{"a" => first1} = map2
first1

```

```elixir
#Updates the map ande extracts the updated elements value 
my_map = %{my_map | a: 5}
%{a: fir} = my_map
fir
```

## Struct

```elixir
defmodule User do
  defstruct username: "", email: "", age: nil
end
```

```elixir
user1 = %User{username: "Ram", email: "abc@gmail.com", age: 21}
```

```elixir
%{username: un} = user1
un
```

```elixir
user1 = %{user1 | email: "ram@gmail.com"}
```
